            <ArticleTitle>Hemodynamic compromise secondary to a mediastinal bronchogenic cyst.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>610-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bronchogenic cysts are not commonly the cause of severe symptoms, and often present only as an abnormality on chest roentgenogram. We report an unusual patient with a mediastinal bronchogenic cyst associated with rapid hemodynamic deterioration secondary to compression of vital structures.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
